## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    V["Video File"] --> FE["extract_frames()"]
    FE --> FD["JPEG Frames Directory"]
    FD --> VE["VideoEngine"]
    VE --> NS["Namespace: video_dir, frame_count, fps"]
    NS --> LLM["LLM generates Python program"]
    LLM --> PRG["Program calls video modules"]
    PRG --> TRK["track() → SAM2VideoPredictor"]
    PRG --> LOC["loc_frame() → GroundingDINO"]
    PRG --> VQA["vqa_frame() → GPT-4o"]
    PRG --> GF["get_frame() → PIL Image"]
    PRG --> RES["result() → final answer"]
```

## Key Design Decisions

1. **SAM 2 Video Predictor** is initialized via [VideoModulesList](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py#964-1089) using the same checkpoint as image mode, just wrapped in `SAM2VideoPredictor` instead of `SAM2ImagePredictor`
2. **Auto-chunking**: `VideoModulesList._auto_chunk_size()` detects GPU VRAM and sets chunk size accordingly (None for ≥24GB, 100 for 16GB, 50 for 8GB)
3. **Video modules delegate** to existing image modules — [VideoLocateModule](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py#840-878) wraps [LocateModule](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py#57-215), [VideoVQAModule](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py#880-923) wraps [VQAModule](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py#216-356)
4. **LLM receives video-specific variables** (`video_dir`, [frame_count](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/video_utils.py#169-181), `fps`) instead of a single [image](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine_utils.py#153-161)

